OL,5,G0120 24 Hours in A&E
OL,6,     FIt's a busy day at King's, as 400
OL,7,     Fpatients are treated in 24 hours.
OL,8,     FPeggy, who's 85, comes in with her
OL,9,     Fdoting husband. And Ben's swollen
OL,10,     Ffinger is more serious than he
OL,11,     Frealises.
OL,12,G0225 24 Hours in A&E
OL,13,     FThis episode focuses on mums.
OL,14,     FEddie, who's 12, has been hit by a
OL,15,     Fcar. It's his fourth visit to A&E
OL,16,     Fon a blue light. Meanwhile, Linda,
OL,17,     Fwho's 64, has had respiratory
OL,18,     Ffailure.
